+## After P8 (relief check in the frames loop)
+
+After `frameReliefSteps` (2) lowerings in one stress episode, if smoothed frame cost (an EWMA of
+0.5 over stressed windows) has closed less than `frameReliefGapShare` (25%) of the gap to the
+budget, the frames loop stops lowering until frames are back near or within budget, and says
+"not relieved by levers". Heat, memory and contention still act.
+
+| p4, burst | quality given up | while janking | flaps / min |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| low | 63% → 63% | 84% → 84% | 0 → 0 |
+| mid | 30% → 7% | 65% → 11% | 0.40 → 0 |
+| high | 23% → 2% | 65% → 8% | 0.80 → 0 |
+
+Jank is unchanged (25%, the burst's own work), as it must be. Heat soak improved as a side effect
+(high: given 17 → 14%, peak 42.9 → 41.1 °C): fewer wasted steps, less heat from re-raising them.
+The low phone's two steps are forced reduced motion and rows-ahead (it sits at its class floors);
+choosing by measured gain per quality is P7. One step instead of two was tried and refused: on the
+heat soak one noisy step is not evidence, and high-phone jank rose from 0 to 55%.
+
+Building P8 also found a ledger bug: a lowering held back by a gesture (invariant 7) was
+published after the loop's pressure had already risen, and the outcome ledger filed it as a floor
+move, so the unhelpful-lever rule never saw it. Fixed in `outcomes.ts`, with a regression test.
